{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{# Battle Summaries: what the speaker knows about the battle underway or just fought, from BattleSummaries.dll (battle_summary).
   SkyrimNet keeps raw hit, spell and combat events out of the dialogue history; this is the summary that stands in
   for them. It renders into the speaker's own prompt only: the render_mode guard above must stay on line 1, and a
   mod decorator cannot be evaluated for an NPC who is neither speaker nor target.
   The lines themselves are written by the DLL from what it recorded (BattleSummaries.ini tunes them); the framing and
   the rule at the end are yours to edit here. #}
{% set battleSummary = battle_summary(npc.UUID) %}
{% if battleSummary.show %}
{% if battleSummary.ongoing %}
**THE BATTLE UNDERWAY (what has happened so far):**
{% else %}
**THE BATTLE FOUGHT {{ upper(battleSummary.age) }} (what actually happened):**
{% endif %}
{% for line in battleSummary.general %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% if length(battleSummary.personal) > 0 %}
What happened to {{ battleSummary.name }} in it:
{% for line in battleSummary.personal %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if length(battleSummary.others) > 0 %}
{% if battleSummary.participant %}Those who fought beside {{ battleSummary.name }}:{% else %}{{ battleSummary.name }} did not fight, but saw it. Those who fought:{% endif %}
{% for line in battleSummary.others %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
This is the true account of the battle, and {{ battleSummary.name }} remembers it this way. {% if battleSummary.team %}{{ battleSummary.name }} and those beside them fought as one party, and {{ battleSummary.name }} reads this account from that side: the outcome belongs to all of them, each helped it in their own way, and who killed or struck the most is no measure of anyone's worth. {{ battleSummary.name }} does not belittle a companion or reproach themselves over their share of the fighting. {{ battleSummary.name }} may feel anything about the battle itself that fits their character, but must not deny{% else %}{{ battleSummary.name }} may feel anything about it that fits their character (pride, shame, gratitude, resentment, bravado), but must not deny{% endif %} or reverse what happened, claim kills or deeds that are not listed, or play down how close to death anyone came or who saved whom. Being struck down is not dying: anyone told as struck down or as having risen again is alive, and nobody died unless the account says they were killed. Do not recite this account or its wording; let it shape what is said, and only when the battle is relevant.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
